# 20261005T163040-1001-192-168-30-104-26668.wav
#
# A 14400 call modec placed through the bench that connected and could
# not be read from the first data symbol: one of fifty that afternoon,
# with nothing wrong on the line.
#
# Figure 4 has the answering modem stop for as long as the caller's
# conditioning signal lasts, here 2.4 s, and the receiver waits that
# out with its loops still ('Modec.QAM.qrFadeHold').  Its symbol clock
# was held at the rate the timing loop stood at on the last symbol
# before the line went quiet -- and a loop's rate is the far end's plus
# the loop's own noise.  Through the answerer's training this one read
# between 3.3326 and 3.3338 samples a symbol about a mean of 3.33315,
# and it stopped on 3.33291.  Over 5760 symbols that is 1.4 samples: the
# answerer's second training came back 0.41 of a symbol from where the
# receiver was looking, the loop was kicked 2400 ppm chasing it, was
# still ringing when B1 arrived, and the data pump was handed a
# receiver at an error of 0.015.  It asked for a retrain three seconds
# later, at a pinned rate that has none to offer.
#
# The clock now coasts through a quiet line on its average over the
# signal before it, and comes back where it left: an error of 0.005
# half a second after the answerer returns, 0.0009 a second after that,
# and data at 0.0005.
#
# Nothing in the text: the far end idles for all of what is kept, and
# the two bytes are the seam.  The recording stops at 22.0 s because
# the far end retrains at 22.2, answering the request the live call
# made at 21.9.
seconds:   22.0
role:      originate
modes:     v32bis
v8:        no
connect:   V32bis 14400
retrains:  0
tolerance: 2
